# Codex Review

Target: branch diff against origin/main

Two reproduced regressions allow previously blocked oracle writes through the hook. The documentation checker and diff whitespace check passed; the full gate was not run in this read-only review.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Recognize prefixed sed invocations before classifying writes — /home/joe/repos/ASTRA/.claude/hooks/guard-oracle.sh:329-333
  With the oracle guard unarmed, `LC_ALL=C sed -i 's/x/y/' tests/golden/probe.hpp` now exits 0, whereas the base hook exits 2. Removing sed from the coarse filter leaves this parser as its only protection, but it treats `LC_ALL=C` as the executable; `command sed` also bypasses it. Normalize ordinary command prefixes before classifying sed so these literal in-place writes still require authorization under [AGENTS.md:27–29](AGENTS.md#L27-L29).

- [P2] Preserve protection for oracle paths outside the session root — /home/joe/repos/ASTRA/.claude/hooks/guard-oracle.sh:353-355
  From a worktree session, `sed -i 's/x/y/' /home/joe/repos/ASTRA/tests/golden/nesc/case1_dragless_sphere.hpp` now passes the unarmed hook because `rel_to_root()` returns `None` for the main checkout. The base hook blocks this same absolute-path write. Check resolved targets against protected paths in the main checkout and other worktrees rather than dropping targets outside `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`; the oracle-authorization rule is not limited to the current worktree ([AGENTS.md:27–29](AGENTS.md#L27-L29)).
